' Two independently renderable diagrams: current and proposed architecture.
' Proposed symbols and file locations below are design recommendations.

@startuml 674-acp-current
title ACP execution today — host agent, separate sandbox capability
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11

package "Engine / graph runtime" {
  component "Graph service composition\napps/web/.../composition.py" as composition
  component "Runtime ACPNode\ngraph_runtime_langgraph/acp.py" as node
  database "Graph runtime store\nACPContinuation + approval" as store
}

package "langgraph-acp — standalone library" {
  component "resume_continuation()\ncontinuation.py" as resume
  component "ACPAgentRegistry\nagent.py" as registry
  component "Reusable provider configuration\nCodex / Claude / OpenCode / Stdio\nconnect() — no invocation context" as provider
  component "connect_over_stdio()\n_stdio.py" as launch
  component "StdioACPClient + JSONRPCPeer\nprotocol, events, diagnostics, cleanup" as client
}

node "Host process execution" {
  component "asyncio subprocess\nACP adapter + agent" as agent
}

package "Engine sandbox capability — separate execution path" {
  component "Capabilities.sandbox\nSandbox.create(SandboxSpec)" as port
  component "ProcessSandbox" as process
  component "SmolvmSandbox" as smolvm
}

composition --> registry : registers host providers
node --> store : save / read continuation
node --> registry : fresh: resolve(agent)
node --> resume : recovery: stored continuation\n+ cwd + MCP + session config
resume --> registry : resolve(continuation.agent)
registry --> provider : returns shared configuration
node --> provider : fresh: connect()
resume --> provider : recovery: connect()
provider --> launch : command, env, launch cwd, handlers
launch --> agent : create_subprocess_exec()
launch --> client : construct + initialize
client <--> agent : ACP JSON-RPC over stdin / stdout\nstderr drained separately
node --> client : session/new or session/load\nthen prompt / events / close
port --> process
port --> smolvm

note right of provider
  Providers hold configuration, not connection state.
  They receive no run, node, workspace or sandbox spec.
  Session cwd is supplied after connection launch.
end note

note right of launch
  CURRENT ENVIRONMENT
  env=None inherits the full host environment.
  Explicit env overlays the full host environment.
end note

note bottom of port
  No ACP provider calls this port today.
  Selecting smolvm does not move graph agents into VMs.
  ProcessSandbox also inherits the full host environment.
  SmolVM already filters its host control environment;
  guest exec receives explicit env / spec secrets.
end note

legend bottom
  Solid arrows = existing calls or data flow.
  This view follows the runtime ACPNode; the minimal library ACPNode
  also resolves a provider and calls connect() without context.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml 674-acp-proposed
title Proposed ACP execution — invocation context + sandbox stdio transport
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam componentBackgroundColor<<added>> #E2F3E6
skinparam componentBackgroundColor<<changed>> #FFF0CC

package "Engine / graph runtime" {
  component "Graph composition / runtime wiring\nconfigured Sandbox backend\nincluding added agents + runner overrides" as composition <<changed>>
  component "Runtime ACPNode\ngraph_runtime_langgraph/acp.py\nresolve context once per invocation" as node <<changed>>
  component "Engine connection context\nrun / node / execution identifiers\nresolved workspace + SandboxSpec" as context <<added>>
  database "Graph runtime store\nACPContinuation + approval" as store
}

package "langgraph-acp — no Engine imports" {
  component "ACPConnectContext\nproposed: context.py\nEngine-neutral base context" as base <<added>>
  component "ACPAgentRegistry\nresolves reusable provider" as registry
  component "resume_continuation(..., context=...)\ncontinuation.py" as resume <<changed>>
  component "ACPAgentProvider.connect(*, context=None)\nagent.py + all built-in providers" as hook <<changed>>
  component "Shared ACP connection factory\nstreams + lifecycle operations\nextracted from _stdio.py" as factory <<added>>
  component "Shared ACP client + JSONRPCPeer\ninitialize / sessions / events / permissions\nbackend-independent cleanup contract" as client <<changed>>
  component "Local stdio provider / launcher\nfiltered host env + explicit configuration\nsubprocess lifecycle implementation" as local <<changed>>
}

package "Engine ACP adapter — proposed provider location" {
  component "SandboxACPProvider\nimplements ACPAgentProvider\nimmutable reusable configuration" as provider <<added>>
}

package "Engine sandbox port / adapters" {
  component "Sandbox.create(spec)\nSandboxInstance.exec(argv, cwd, env)\ncopy_in / copy_out / destroy" as port
  component "Sandbox connection lifecycle\nowns sandbox context\nclose or setup failure => destroy" as lifetime <<added>>
  component "ProcessSandbox\nexplicit host env allowlist\n+ command env + spec secrets" as process <<changed>>
  component "SmolvmSandbox\nverify clean guest environment\nACP-compatible stream size" as smolvm <<changed>>
}

node "SmolVM guest — disposable workspace" {
  folder "/workspace\ncopied from resolved host workspace" as workspace
  component "Installed ACP adapter + agent\ncodex-acp OR claude-agent-acp\nalready pinned in guest image" as guest
}

composition --> node : configure selected backend and registry
node --> store : save / read continuation
node --> context : build once
context ..|> base : extends
node --> resume : recovery: continuation + same context
resume --> registry : resolve stored agent
registry --> hook : provider contract
node --> hook : fresh: connect(context=context)
hook --> provider : sandbox provider selected\ncontext forwarded on fresh AND resume
hook --> local : local provider selected
provider --> port : create(context.sandbox_spec)\nexec(guest command, relative cwd, explicit env)
provider --> lifetime : owns until client.close()
lifetime --> port : exit context / destroy()
port --> process : process backend
port --> smolvm : VM backend
smolvm --> guest : exec installed adapter\nno runtime npm install
provider --> factory : sandbox streams + lifecycle
local --> factory : subprocess streams + lifecycle
factory --> client : construct + initialize
client <--> guest : ACP JSON-RPC over sandbox exec stdio\nstderr drained separately
guest --> workspace : reads / writes guest files

note right of context
  ADD in graph runtime / Engine adapter:
  typed SandboxSpec extension and per-node resolver.
  Do not store invocation state on shared providers.
  Do not serialize secrets into continuations or events.
end note

note right of hook
  CHANGE in langgraph-acp:
  propagate context through fresh and resume paths,
  built-in providers and minimal library ACPNode.
  Direct connect() calls still work with context=None.
  Custom providers must adopt the new signature.
end note

note right of provider
  ADD at the Engine adapter boundary:
  composition injects the selected Sandbox backend
  and explicit guest command configuration.
  map host workspace to sandbox workspace.
  exec cwd is workspace-relative;
  ACP new/load cwd is the guest absolute path.
  Apply translation on both new and loaded sessions.
  Client close / handshake failure exits owned sandbox.
  Preserve permission and elicitation handlers.
end note

note right of factory
  EXTRACT from _stdio.py:
  protocol handling must not require subprocess-only
  returncode / terminate / kill methods.
  Sandbox cleanup must stop the guest, not just its CLI.
  Preserve the existing 8 MiB ACP message budget.
end note

note bottom of process
  ENVIRONMENT POLICY — all launch paths
  Inherit only named approved variables.
  Explicit configuration is a deliberate grant.
  SandboxSpec.secrets wins over conflicting command env.
  Guest PATH / HOME / temp paths use guest values.
  Verify the entire effective agent environment,
  including image/runtime defaults, in tests.
end note

note bottom of workspace
  RECOVERY / INTEGRATION BOUNDARIES
  Disposable VM deletion also deletes agent session state.
  Passing context alone does not make session/load durable.
  Define persistence before claiming restart recovery;
  unavailable state must fail explicitly, never start fresh silently.
  Result export remains explicit copy_out, without automatic host merge.
  Host MCP reachability needs validation or the planned bridge (#678).
  Credential lifecycle remains follow-up #676; acceptance uses explicit test secrets.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  | <#E2F3E6> Green | Proposed addition |
  | <#FFF0CC> Amber | Existing component to change |
  | White | Existing component / capability to reuse |
  Dashed triangle arrows = implements / extends; solid arrows = call / data flow.
  Proposed names and locations are planning decisions, not implemented code.
  Acceptance: real Codex AND Claude nodes complete inside SmolVM;
  tests assert the full environment key set and cleanup on failure / cancellation.
endlegend
@enduml
